From abb55717e664c3d714a7aa1cb5858000c74c6fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:23:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] nemotron: checkpoint prompt passes run the NVFP4
 experts in 128-pair by 128-column tiles

A pass of 128 rows or more (ck.prompt_tokens) plans its routed and shared experts in items of 128 pairs
(ck.prompt_tile) and runs them on tf_ck4_up_relu2_prompt and tf_ck4_down_f32_prompt: a block takes one item of one
expert by 128 columns, eight warps of 64 rows by 32 columns over a four-step cp.async pipeline, inputs through
ldmatrix, and the next unit's first steps load under this one's epilogue. Each output keeps the decode warp's
block-scaled MMA chain over K steps in order and its epilogue, so prompt rows are byte-equal to decode rows. Calls under
128 rows keep the 16-pair warps (and verify windows the _few ones). `tf-cuda-test checkpoint` compares both directions
with the decode warps at 258 pairs over 2 experts [192, 256] and 28,800 pairs over 96 experts [1344, 1024].
